Description: Clear the VP2 decoder's rings through a surface of their own
 nv84_create_decoder zeroes parts of its H.264 macroblock and VP rings
 with clear_render_target, on an nv50_surface it fills in over a miptree
 made up around each ring's bo. Since pipe_surface became a plain
 template the nv50 clear builds its own surface from the template, which
 drops the ring's offset and size and divides by the made-up miptree's
 unset fields. Split the clear into a function that takes an nv50_surface
 as it is, call that from the decoder, and zero the made-up miptree and
 surface before filling them in.
